# Spec-Driven Development

## Required gate

- New or changed product behavior requires a related specification in
  `docs/specs/` with `status: approved`.
- Do not implement a specification with `draft`, `in_review`, or `superseded`
  status.
- Read `docs/sdd/lifecycle.md`, `docs/sdd/roles.md`,
  `docs/sdd/decision-authority.md`, and `docs/sdd/agents.yml` before working
  on a feature specification.
- Run `npm run sdd:validate` whenever a specification changes.

## Responsibilities

- Keep one assigned SDD role per deliverable.
- When starting a dedicated chat or launching a subagent for an SDD role,
  read [`docs/sdd/agents.yml`](docs/sdd/agents.yml) and use that role's
  `model` and `effort`. Do not invent or substitute a model unless a human
  overrides the assignment in the current prompt.
- The `human_approver` role is never an LLM.
- An intake adapter may create or update drafts but cannot approve them.
- A specification author cannot approve its own specification.
- A delivery agent implements only the approved scope.
- A validation agent compares acceptance criteria to tests and recorded
  evidence, but cannot approve its own work.
- A named human is the only approver of a specification.
- Ask the human about missing business and security decisions. Leave those
  items `TBD`.
- Decide missing design and technical how as a senior engineer, record the
  choice in the specification, and promote recurring visual decisions into
  `docs/design.md`. See `docs/sdd/decision-authority.md`.

## Contract hierarchy

- An approved feature specification is the source of truth for that feature.
- `docs/product.md`, `docs/design.md`, `docs/api.md`, and
  `docs/database.md` are durable global contracts, not replacements for a
  feature specification.
- Add a delta to the feature specification first, then update an affected
  global contract as part of the delivery.
- If business scope or security policy is ambiguous, incomplete, or
  conflicts with a global contract, return it to review. Do not infer
  missing business or security decisions.
- If only design or technical how is missing, decide it, record it, and
  continue. Do not ask the human for visual details that follow the
  consolidating design system.

## Intake

- The only request source is a human prompt in an agent conversation.
- Record `source_kind: human_prompt` and
  `source_reference: chat-YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>`.
- Do not create specifications from GitHub Issues, Kanban cards, webhooks,
  or other systems.
- Do not add a channel-specific workflow, secret, credential, or integration
  unless a human updates `docs/sdd/configuration.md`.
